# QA dogfood session artifacts (screenshots from browser probes, 2026-09-18).
# Session output, not source. Also in .assetsignore so wrangler static
# assets never uploads it (wrangler does NOT honor .gitignore).
/dogfood-output/
# Session scratch (did not make the cut for the demo, but are here for
# the record; they are ignored and deleted after each deploy)
*.log
*.bak
*.tmp
*.DS_Store
# Local secret files. 2026-10-04: .dev.vars was already excluded from the
# ASSET bundle (.assetsignore) so it could never ship, but it was NOT in
# .gitignore - so the file wrangler dev reads secrets from was one
# `git add -A` away from being committed. Same shape as the .orig/.head gap
# closed above: the deploy side excluded it, the git side did not.
# Prefer `wrangler secret put`, which never touches disk at all.
.dev.vars
.dev.vars.*
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
secrets.json
# Editor / merge backup files. 2026-10-04: commit 243332e committed four
# 304-line copies of mcp/README.md (HEAD-readme.md, HEAD-copy.md,
# mcp/README.md.orig, mcp/README.md.head) instead of nothing - the real
# edit was already in b25033a. *.md does NOT match README.md.orig (the
# suffix is .orig, not .md), so these also needed an .assetsignore twin.
*.orig
*.head
*~
# Whole-file snapshots dumped in the repo root by a past session.
HEAD-*.md
# 2026-10-04 cleanup of the remaining root scratch. tmp_head_readme.md was
# another copy of the MCP README; claude-cli-1.0.5.tgz was a downloaded
# npm package that the deploy excludes already treated as a public-asset
# leak. Neither belongs in the repo.
tmp_*.md
*.tgz
# Session transcripts dropped in the root. The tracked planning .txt files
# (PLANNING-TODO-*, SECURITY-FIXES-PLAN) are real project docs and are NOT
# matched here - this rule is anchored to the root and only covers the
# "Freebuff ...txt" scratch a chat session leaves behind.
/Freebuff*.txt
scratch.md
scratch.json
tmp/
